  "rules": {
    "objective": "Complete a winning hand: one identical pair (ngán) and three pairs of tiles whose spots add up to 10 or 20 (counting the 4-2 tile as 3 spots).",
    "gameplay": "1. Setup: Build wall 4 high by 8 wide; first player takes 8 tiles, second takes 7.\n2. Turn: Optionally take a face-up discard (if it completes your hand you win); then draw one tile from the wall. If the drawn tile completes your hand you win; otherwise discard one tile face up.\n3. Winning: First to announce a complete hand collects the pot.",
    "keyRules": [
      "Winning hand has one identical pair (ngán) plus three pairs totaling 10 or 20 pips",
      "The 4-2 tile counts as three spots, not six",
      "You may take one discard and draw one from the wall each turn"
    ],
    "hasPlaceholders": false
